Add public resetQueues() method to FlashMessageService.

FlashMessageService (SingletonInterface) accumulates flash message
queues in the protected `$flashMessageQueues` array. Under PHP-FPM
this state dies with the process. Under long-running runtimes the
queues persist, causing flash messages from a previous request to
appear in subsequent requests for unrelated users.

Add a public `resetQueues()` method so the accumulated state can be
cleared without reaching into protected properties.

This follows the precedent set by PageRenderer, AssetCollector, and
MetaTagManagerRegistry which already expose public state management
methods (getState/updateState).

diff --git a/Classes/Messaging/FlashMessageService.php b/Classes/Messaging/FlashMessageService.php
--- a/Classes/Messaging/FlashMessageService.php
+++ b/Classes/Messaging/FlashMessageService.php
@@ -48,4 +48,15 @@
         }
         return $this->flashMessageQueues[$identifier];
     }
+
+    /**
+     * Resets all flash message queues.
+     *
+     * Useful for long-running PHP runtimes where the singleton instance
+     * persists across requests and queued messages must not leak.
+     */
+    public function resetQueues(): void
+    {
+        $this->flashMessageQueues = [];
+    }
 }
